  "description": "This walk visits a lighthouse located on the north coast of Sutherland. You can start the walk from the car park at Totegan and follow a trail north to the lighthouse.Along the way, you will enjoy expansive views over the Atlantic Ocean, with the dramatic cliffs and rocky shoreline providing a striking backdrop. The lighthouse itself sits at the tip of the headland, offering panoramic vistas of the surrounding coastline. Wildlife is abundant in the area, with seabirds often seen nesting on the cliffs and occasional sightings of seals along the shore.",
